      "id": 21295,
      "name": "TheJayMann",
      "username": "TheJayMann",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/thejaymann/{size}/2261_2.png",
      "created_at": "2011-08-13T23:05:24.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I was playing last night with Absolute Zero, with my friend as Ra, against Baron Blade (I was easing him into the game).  I had set up Null-Point Calibration Unit, Isothermic Transducer, Coolant Blast, and Focused Apertures.  I had some fire damage already stored on Coolant Blast.  When Baron’s turn came up, he played Slash and Burn.  As I read the card step by step, I explained that he got damanged four melee.  Then, as soon as I said that I would recieve six fire damage, he started laughing for a good five minutes or so.  Afterwards I end up having him “power me up” on his turn, followed then by Hoarfire (choosing two cold against Baron Blade, two Fire against myself, and then one Cold and Fire against myself, which ended up powering Coolant Blast to eleven.  After that round, I believe Baron went from a full thirty to only two.  Oh, and he wants you to attend Ohiocon (or whatever it’s called in Mid Ohio in January).</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
